Method: phase-aware single-slab retrieval (z=(1-r)/(1+r), n from unwrapped phase of t(1+z)/2)
-> compact complex-Lorentz family fit (passive sqrt branch) -> linear geometry map to the
family's physical parameters (4 features + intercept, ridge=1e-06) -> slab forward
model on the provided wavelength grid. No interpolation/surrogate APIs used for held-out transfer.
The map targets the family parameters retrieved from the calibration spectra (leave-one-out
n,z RMSE = 0.220 for the selected family).
Limitation: the geometry->parameter map is trained on only 6 calibration samples (4 features +
intercept => 1 spare degree of freedom per parameter; leave-one-out used for validation).
Held-out samples lie at or slightly beyond the calibration feature ranges (H1 rod_length), so
the map extrapolates mildly; per-parameter map uncertainty is the dominant source of held-out
error.
